# A children's book in Russian: детский, книжный, дождливый
subtitle: "Дети → детский, книга → книжный, дождь → дождливый, известный → неизвестный: how Russian makes adjectives, at the launch of Masha's guidebook for children."
tags: ["russian","russian adjectives","word formation","детский","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/word-building","vocabulary/culture"]
thumb: "band \"One noun, one new adjective\" stamp \"-СК- -Н-\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Nobody's things in Russian: ничей, ничто, кто-либо","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/212-russian-nobodys-things.cast"}

## A children's book in Russian: детский, книжный, дождливый
